## 2. Problem restatement and scope

Users annotate points/polygons/masks on 2D images and volumes (multi-channel, time series, int/float samples, physical calibration, up to ≥3 GB per file) across instruments; projects move between machines via ordinary shared storage. Minimum workflow: create project → import (originals untouched) → inspect metadata/provenance → navigate/adjust display → annotate → save → close → reopen elsewhere → export annotation table/overlay + small derived image → verify what transformed and what did not. Out of minimum scope: in-place source modification, cloud collaboration, automatic segmentation/registration, DICOM services. **[PC: boundary = brief §3, §4]**

Success criteria for v1 (testable): (a) reopen on a second machine reproduces geometry to float64 exactness; (b) display-setting edits provably leave sample values unchanged; (c) kill during save leaves the previous project state loadable; (d) unsupported file import leaves the project openable and stores the raw metadata. **[PC]**

