## 9. Minimum workflow, mapped

1. **Create project** — empty bundle + manifest v1. **[PC]**
2. **Import** — adapter probe → axes/calibration confirmation dialog showing raw metadata verbatim (F3/F4) → identity hash → manifest entry; originals never touched. Ambiguous axes (Q/Modulo) force the explicit map/exclude decision here. **[EF S1, S4]**
3. **Inspect metadata/provenance** — metadata panel renders the structured fields plus the raw block; every import decision and calibration edit is listed with old/new values and reason. Keyboard-focusable, text-legible (accessibility §11).
4. **Navigate & adjust display** — channel toggles, window/level, slice/time stepping; all keyboard operable; display state visibly labeled "display only". **[EF S8]**
5. **Annotate** — points/polygons/masks with styles; undo/redo per §4 (stroke grouping, cap 100, reset on dimension change — contract copied from the merged napari fix **[EF S2, S3]**); scope selector per record.
6. **Save** — journal append + manifest `os.replace` (W2); close is safe at any point.
7. **Reopen elsewhere** — relocation by hash (§7); missing sources render as `reference_missing` placeholders with annotations intact.
8. **Export** — (a) annotation table (CSV/JSON, coordinates in voxel + a columns block with calibration, scope fields, source hash); (b) overlay PNG/WebP with a sidecar JSON of the exact display mapping used (honesty: overlay encodes view state, table does not); (c) small derived image (downsample/crop/resample) written with a derivation record `{source_hash, operation, parameters, output_hash}`; a geometric transform/resample is a **distinct recorded operation type**, never a side effect of viewing. **[PC]**
9. **Verify** — each export receipt lists: what moved (derived image geometry, dtype, origin), what did not (annotation coordinates remain in source voxel space; source hash unchanged), and how to re-verify (recompute sha256; spot-check source values under annotations). OME-ROI XML export (opportunity §12) carries scope + transform in an interoperable form **[EF S5]**.

