## 10. Support boundary and failure semantics

**Tested/maintained at v1** **[PC]**: OME-TIFF (classic + BigTIFF) via tifffile; plain multi-page TIFF (uint/float, uncompressed or deflate/packbits/LZW) with mandatory axis+calibration confirmation; Zarr v2/v3 stores (read); PNG ≤64 MB for small 2D imports.
**Best-effort, opt-in flag recorded in provenance** **[PC]**: other tifffile-readable vendor formats (ImageJ hyperstack, LSM, NDPI, STK…), because **[EF S1/F2]** documents corruption/wrong-metadata modes in exactly these; the import dialog shows the specific README-documented risk for the detected format.
**Out at v1**: OME-TIFF *writing* beyond single-series, DICOM, multi-file vendor databases (NDTiff pyramids), stitching (BIF/Trestle tiles are decoded but not stitched — same as tifffile's own boundary **[EF S1]**).
**Failure without destruction**: adapter probes read-only and raise typed errors before any manifest mutation; the attempted import becomes a `failed_import` provenance record retaining the raw metadata block verbatim; project stays openable (journal/manifest unaffected); user choice recorded ("keep record / delete record"). No universal-format claim is made anywhere in UI or docs. **[PC]** on **[EF S1]**

