## 11. Accessibility and operability

All tools keyboard-reachable: tool cycling (e.g., `V/P/L/M`), slice/time arrows, `Ctrl+Z`/`Ctrl+Shift+Z` (precedent: napari binds undo in keybindings.py **[EF S3]**), Enter to commit a point, Esc to cancel in-progress geometry, keyboard-adjustable window/level. Metadata, errors, and calibration warnings are plain text in a focusable log panel plus a status line (screen-reader legible; no color-only signaling); high-contrast annotation styles; focus indicators on all panels. Original-vs-derived distinction: derived views get a persistent border badge + tab tint + a one-line derivation sentence in the status bar. **[PC]**

