## 12. Opportunity and alternatives

- **Opportunity (recommended)**: OME-ROI XML export. It maps 1:1 onto our record model (Point/Polygon/Polyline/Rectangle/Ellipse/Mask, `TheZ/TheT/TheC` scope semantics, 6-value affine Transform, text/styles) **[EF S5]**, immediately interops with ImageJ/OMERO ecosystems, and forces us to keep the scope semantics honest. Cost: an XML writer + schema spot-tests. **[PC]**
- **Alternative for portability**: Zarr/NGFF as the bundle's derived-image format from day one (chunked, cloud-tolerant; tifffile already targets NGFF 0.4/0.5 in zarr output per its 2026 revision notes **[EF S1]**), with PNG only as a convenience render. Deferred for v1 masks (plain chunked files suffice) to bound the dependency surface. **[PC, deferred — lead L2]**
- **Alternative for reading**: `bioio`/`aicsimageio` instead of tifffile — rejected v1 because tifffile's documented limitation list **[EF S1]** is exactly the kind of explicit boundary a 6-person team can test; revisit if OME-TIFF coverage proves insufficient.
- **Not adopted** (kept as leads): array-`__setitem__`-interception undo (napari PR #3155 — unmerged, API-risky **[EF S6]**, L5); single-file SQLite project (§6).

