## 13. Performance plan vs. the 3 GB target

Envelope: 8 cores, 16 GB RAM, optional GPU; engineering target only — **no component here is evidence of meeting it** (brief §4). Plan **[EI on EF S1, S9]**: viewport-driven tile reads only (tifffile tile/page reads + dask/zarr chunk views are the precedent mechanism, F1); single decode per tile into the LRU cache; pyramids from file SubIFDs when present, else cached derived overviews (recorded as derived data); window/level applied on the cached display copy at render time; cooperative cancellation tokens threaded through tile loops; progress = tiles done/total. Manifest-save latency is independent of image size (annotations only). The unbounded-copy hazards to police: whole-file `imread`, float64 upcasting of sample caches, and per-undo full-volume snapshots (napari's lesson generalized: snapshot the *slice*, not the array **[EF S3]**).

**Validation [PV — all UNEXECUTED]**: W3 3 GB OME-TIFF: peak RSS < ~3 GB while paging a 10-minute scripted tour; W4 bundle reopen+relocation on a second machine with hash verification; W5 display-edit isolation + float64 round-trip test; W6 OS-level kill-during-save dirty-shutdown test (extends W2); W7 Q/Modulo-axis corpus test (F4 consequence).

