## 14. Assumptions, unsupported cases, risks

- **Assumption [EI]**: tifffile's read path over OME-TIFF keeps per-tile RSS bounded — supported by its documented strip/tile/zarr access **[EF S1]** but not yet measured by us (**W3 UNEXECUTED**).
- **Assumption [EI]**: sha256-at-import is an acceptable identity cost (one-time, ~10–20 s/3 GB). If not, deferred hashing + size+mtime pre-check is the fallback **[PC]**.
- **Unsupported case 1**: images with Modulo/`Q` axes — annotations blocked until explicit mapping (F4); no silent 5D reinterpretation.
- **Unsupported case 2**: uncalibrated sources — workspace shows "uncalibrated"; physical exports refuse or stamp `uncalibrated` (user choice recorded). **[PC]**
- **Unsupported case 3**: float32-only calibration in source files — stored as original, workspace copy upcast to float64 with a warning record (**W1**).
- **Risk**: napari's `contrast_limits`-style defaults (S8, shallow capture) suggest auto-windowing on first view; if we adopt auto-window we must persist it as view state *with provenance of the percentile parameters* or reopen fidelity suffers. **[EI, low confidence — deeper napari docs capture needed, lead L6]**
- **Risk**: journal corruption on shared storage without fsync guarantees (NFS/SMB). Bounded alternative: fsync + directory fsync + `verify_project` repair from journal+snapshot (W2 mechanism); worst case the bundle loses the last commands, never the manifest. **[EI]**

